Avoid f64::algebraic_add/algebraic_mul (unstable, feature `float_algebraic`,
stabilizes in Rust 1.98.0 - see rust-lang/rust#136469 and #157029). Our
pinned rust-bin toolchain is older, so stable rustc rejects these calls.

Replace with f64::mul_add(), which is stable and, on the avx2+fma/avx512f
multiversion targets this function already dispatches to, compiles to a
single fused multiply-add instruction - same op count as the algebraic
form, just without the cross-iteration reassociation hint that would let
LLVM auto-vectorize the reduction. Negligible cost here (FIR resample is
a tiny fraction of jgenesis's per-frame budget).

TODO: drop this patch once RUST_BIN_VERSION >= 1.98.0.

--- a/common/jgenesis-common/src/audio/fir_resampler.rs
+++ b/common/jgenesis-common/src/audio/fir_resampler.rs
@@ -144,7 +144,7 @@
         for (i, coefficient) in coefficients.iter().copied().enumerate() {
             let input_idx = samples[0].idx + i;
             for (ch, sum) in sums.iter_mut().enumerate() {
-                *sum = sum.algebraic_add(coefficient.algebraic_mul(samples[ch].buffer[input_idx]));
+                *sum = coefficient.mul_add(samples[ch].buffer[input_idx], *sum);
             }
         }
